jmp-ai-music-player (1.2.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Profile panel no longer dead-ends on a track that has no profile yet.
    It now offers "Measure this track" whenever a measurement could really
    produce one, and starts the library's existing background analyser
    (`psycho_features.py` then `psycho_profile.py`).  No new measurement mode
    was added, and the job writes only the profile database, the generated
    `Playlists/Psycho/` lists and their reports — never the audio.
  * `psycho_job.needed()` now compares the live inventory against the database,
    so a file that arrived after the last run counts as work: the footer's
    profiles chip reads "13,199 / 13,200 · 1 track has never been measured"
    instead of hiding itself, and Settings → Sound profile is no longer stuck
    on "everything measured".  A finished library still shows no chip.
  * A track that cannot be measured says why instead of leaving the missing
    button unexplained: a failed decode ("the audio could not be decoded"),
    a format the analyser never reads (SPC, SID, tracker modules), or a
    profile whose axes have not been built yet.
  * An audio row whose decode failed (every axis NULL) is treated as "no
    profile", so the net diagram is no longer drawn empty without an
    explanation.
  * No tag, playlist, journal or audio file is written.

