jmp-ai-music-player (1.2.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The playing track now says what *it* still lacks.  "No profile for this
    track yet" named one gap without saying whether the same file also has no
    lyrics, and the panels only ever quoted library-wide counts.  A listener
    looking at one song now sees that song's state: the now-playing strip
    prints "not analysed · no lyrics" under the artist, the Profile panel
    carries a chip per gap ("not analysed", "no lyrics yet", "lyrics out of
    date"), and the Lyrics panel's note adds the missing analysis and whether
    a local transcriber is installed at all.
  * One computation answers all of them: Engine.track_state(rel) reports
    profile, lyrics, lyrics_stale (a transcription from an earlier version of
    the file), the missing list and a ready sentence.  It is read-only and
    cached per file stamp plus the two database stamps (main file and -wal, so
    a transcription really invalidates it), which is what lets the 2 s status
    poll carry it.  /api/status, /api/psycho, /api/lyrics and the chat's
    no-profile/no-lyrics answers all read the same result.
  * A track that was never measured no longer claims "partly estimated";
    that label now requires an existing profile.  A track that is fully
    analysed and transcribed shows no gap at all.  Nothing is written to an
    audio file, a tag, a playlist or a journal by any of these reads.

