jmp-ai-music-player (1.2.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The cover no longer silently disappears.  A Debian install runs on the
    distribution Python, which has no mutagen unless python3-mutagen is
    installed; tagedit swallowed that ImportError, so every cover looked
    absent and the strip kept its music-note icon even for a file with a real
    embedded picture.  The reader now separates "this track has no art" from
    "the reader failed": the first still answers 404 and keeps the icon, the
    second answers 500 with the reason, is written to server-errors.log and
    shows up in Diagnostics.  art_state() reports the same distinction in the
    tag editor, and artwork_reader() tells the page which interpreter and
    mutagen version it is running on.
  * The cover request no longer depends on a track the chat queued.
    GET /api/status now derives the library-relative path from the file mpv is
    really playing, so a playlist, `music play` or a media key after a restart
    also gets a picture; /api/status additionally carries art
    (embedded|folder|none) from the inventory, so the page can tell a missing
    cover from a failed read without opening the audio file.
  * The page asks through fetch instead of an <img>, so the HTTP status is
    known: a 404 is quiet, a 500 is recorded in the client error list and
    named in the cover's tooltip.  The blob is shown only after it decoded.
  * The running version is now visible in the app.  lib/chat/version.py reads
    the VERSION file that ships next to the code (/usr/lib/jmp/VERSION in the
    package, /opt/music/VERSION in the image, application/VERSION in a
    checkout) and nothing else keeps a copy: the window shows it next to the
    name and in its title, /api/state carries it, Diagnostics prints it with
    the Python and mutagen it runs on, the chat answers /version and "which
    version of the app am I running", and the HTTP Server header and the
    planner's User-Agent identify themselves with it instead of a hardcoded
    1.0.  A file without a plain number (the host installer's app=… record) is
    ignored rather than shown as a version.

