jmp-ai-music-player (1.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The now-playing strip shows the cover art.  The box left of the title had
    a fixed music-note icon and never asked for a picture, so a library with
    6,351 embedded covers and 1,211 folder covers looked like it had none.  A
    new endpoint, GET /api/cover?rel=…, answers the real bytes: the picture
    inside the file first, then the album's cover.jpg/cover.png/folder.jpg (the
    names the scanner already records), with the MIME sniffed from the image
    rather than trusted from a name, because the answer carries nosniff.  A
    track without artwork answers 404 and the box keeps its note icon, which is
    what the chiptune shelves and the loose singles get.  Nothing is written:
    tagedit.art_bytes() only reads, and it refuses any path that resolves
    outside the library.
  * The page asks once per track and keeps the request cheap: an <img> cannot
    send the API header, so the token travels in ?t= like the page's own (query
    strings never reach the logs), and the picture is only shown after it
    really decoded, so an unreadable cover falls back to the icon instead of a
    broken frame.  A cover written from the tag editor is picked up on the next
    status poll.
  * New headless checks: check_cover covers embedded-before-folder, a broken
    embedded picture, no artwork, the path guard, the endpoint with and without
    the token, the page wiring and that showing a cover rewrites no file.

