jmp-ai-music-player (1.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the GNOME global media keys actually reach the player.  A binding
    used to call "music-cli", but a desktop shortcut starts outside the shell
    that started the app: a source install, a .deb and a player inside a
    container can all expose a different "music-cli", so the key drove the
    wrong socket (or none) while the shortcut still looked installed.
  * Bindings now call "jmp-media-action".  It tries the running server's
    loopback API first (the URL the window or the MPRIS agent recorded), then
    the MPRIS player on the session bus, and only then music-cli.  --probe
    reports which route would work right now.
  * Settings -> Playback -> Global media keys gained a Test button that shows
    the live route, and it names a key that another GNOME shortcut already
    owns instead of claiming the binding works.
  * An entry left by 1.2.0/1.2.1 (right F5-F8, but calling music-cli) is shown
    as "outdated" and rewritten in place when the window opens or Install is
    clicked.  Nothing new is installed silently: only JMP's own bindings are
    touched, and only to point them at the helper.
  * Installing no longer reports success when the desktop refused the grab.
    gsd-media-keys and mutter can fail a grab silently; the install reads the
    user journal and says so with the exact reason.
  * The shortcut log line carries the route but never the API token, and the
    log file is created private (0600).
  * No music file, tag or playlist is touched; a key press still runs exactly
    one transport command.

