jmp-ai-music-player (1.1.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The media row of this keyboard is stop, rewind, play/pause, forward on
    F5-F8 -- not the toggle/stop/prev/next order assumed so far.  That is why
    play/pause restarted the track (it was mapped to "previous", which seeks to
    0:00) and rewind stopped the music (it was mapped to "stop").
  * The mapping therefore follows the printed row; the same wrong guess is now
    correctable without a rebuild through
    ~/.config/julians-music-app/media-keys.json or JMP_MEDIA_KEYS.
  * The key log is timestamped and also records the action a press became and
    the player's own answer, so a key that does not do what it should is
    visible in ~/.cache/julians-music-app/media-keys.log without repeating it
    from memory.
  * Plain F5-F8 reach only the focused window (Wayland has no global key
    observation); for the keys to work in every application the keyboard row
    has to send real XF86Audio* keys, which the desktop already routes to the
    player through MPRIS.  The README explains both routes.

